\normalsize
\noindent My research focuses on exploring the cosmic frontier using astronomical instrumentation, multi-messenger astrophysics, and standard siren cosmology.
In this research proposal, I will describe how my research experience and leadership has prepared me for a \Position\ at \Institute.
\hrule
\begin{tcolorbox}[
  colback=blue!5!white,      % Interior background color
  colframe=blue!75!black,    % Outer border color
  title=Early Career Contributions % Top box title
]
  \begin{itemize}[noitemsep, topsep=0pt, leftmargin=1em]
    \item Commissioning the focal plane array of LSST-Camera, testing and integrating multi-object and integral-field spectroscopic instruments.
    \item Leading searches for electromagnetic counterparts to gravitational wave mergers using Vera C. Rubin Observatory, and observing campaigns using other photometric and spectroscopic instruments.
    \item Measuring $H_0$ using the dark siren method and the Dark Energy Legacy Volume Explorer galaxy catalog.
  \end{itemize}

  % Connects lower box section with a title bar
  
\end{tcolorbox}
% \vspace{0.15cm}
% This focus is rooted in by three distinct pillars: building cutting-edge astronomical instrumentation, leading observing campaigns to search for the electromagnetic counterparts to gravitational-wave mergers, and performing inference on electromagnetic and gravitational-wave data to achieve robust cosmological constraints.
% These three pillars reflect the expertise I will bring to \Institute, where each research activity is not viewed as separate, but as three legs of one research program, strongest when pursued together. 
